  "Id": 1850,
  "Title": "Nursing trends",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Dr David Arthur writes about the evolving nursing trends in Pakistan.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<p>In a recent op-ed by Dr David Arthur, dean of AKU's School of Nursing and Midwifery, he says that a strategic shift is under way that suggests that there has never been a better time to be a nurse in the country. Dr Arthur is also a representative of Nursing Now in Pakistan.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dawn.com/news/1471513/nursing-trends\">Read more</a></p><p><p><strong>About Nursing Now</strong></p><p>Nursing Now is a global, three-year long campaign run in collaboration with the World Health Organization and the International Council of Nurses. The campaign aims to raise the status and profile of nursing and midwifery professions.  </p><p>In January 2019, Pakistan also became part of this campaign joining forces with nurse leaders from around the world.   </p><a href=\"https://www.nursingnow.org/\"><p>Learn more<br/></p><br/></a></p>",
